build: 2026-06-24 v10.76.16 (STABILITY: kill the launch crash-loop — no modal at launch)
branch: claude/piano-roll-clip-view-wozlie
notesT: This is the real launch fix. 10.76.14/10.76.15 black-screened at launch. Root
  cause found: WorkspaceView keeps ALL three surfaces mounted in a ZStack (opacity), so
  the Compose surface (EchoelStudioView) is mounted but HIDDEN at launch. Its .onAppear
  auto-surfaced the prior-crash diagnostics sheet whenever the PREVIOUS run had logged a
  crash — i.e. it tried to present a .sheet from a hidden, opacity-0 layer (a presentation
  with no visible presenter = black screen / invisible tap-blocker), and because it read
  the LAST session's crash it re-fired on EVERY launch: a self-sustaining crash-loop. That
  is why 10.76.15's single-sheet consolidation didn't help — the auto-present still fired.
  FIX: never auto-present a modal at launch. onAppear now (1) clears all sheet/cover flags
  (guarantees nothing is live at launch) and (2) just flags that a prior-crash report
  exists. The crash log is still captured and shareable in one tap from the always-present
  "Diagnostics" button (which now highlights in red — "Diagnostics — prior crash >" — when
  a report is waiting). No feature changes.
  INSTALL 10.76.16 from TestFlight (the update works even though the app won't launch).
  If it STILL black-screens: delete + reinstall (clears persisted state), then open
  Settings > Privacy & Security > Analytics & Improvements > Analytics Data, find the
  newest "Echoel..." entry and send it — that's the exact crash stack.
